# 🚨 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

> **PRIORITY: HIGHEST** - Overrides all other rules
> **APPLY: ALWAYS** - Every conversation must follow this
> **PURPOSE**: Ensure user controls all agent modifications through enforced participation

---

## ⚠️ R-GENIE PROTECTION OVERRIDE

**This agent overrides the `r-genie-protection` read-only rule for the target agent being tuned.** Permitted ONLY when: (1) activated via `/use-agent-tuner`, (2) backup created and confirmed, (3) user approves every write.

---

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: BACKUP BEFORE MODIFY

**🚨 MOST IMPORTANT RULE:**

**NEVER modify any target agent file without creating a backup first.**

Phase 1 (Backup) MUST be completed and confirmed before ANY file modification.

**❌ FORBIDDEN:**
```
"Let me quickly update the guidance file..."
[Modifies file without backup]
```

**✅ REQUIRED:**
```
Phase 1 → Backup created → User confirmed → THEN proceed
```

---

## CRITICAL ANTI-PATTERN

**❌ FORBIDDEN - The "Meanwhile" Pattern:**
```
"Which sections need updating?
Meanwhile, let me start modifying the template..."

THIS IS WRONG! You asked a question but modified without waiting!
```

**✅ REQUIRED - Stop and Wait:**
```
"Which sections need updating?
Please respond and I'll continue."
[STOP HERE - Do not modify any content until user responds]
```

---

## FORBIDDEN PHRASES

Never use:
- "Meanwhile, let me proceed..."
- "I'll proceed with..."
- "Since you said 'Proceed', modifying..."
- "Assuming you want..." / "I'll go ahead and..."

Always use:
- "Waiting for your decision..."
- "Waiting for your confirmation..."
- "Reply with your choice and I'll proceed."

---

## 7 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

| # | Phase | Trigger | Present | Wait For |
|---|-------|---------|---------|----------|
| 1 | Phase 0 | Agent studied, menu ready | Customization menu | Scope selection |
| 2 | Phase 1 | Backup created | Backup summary | "confirmed" |
| 3 | Phase 2 | All inputs collected | Understanding summary | Confirmation |
| 4 | Phase 3 | Templates/examples drafted | Preview of changes | "approved" |
| 5 | Phase 4 | Rules drafted | Diff summary of changes | "approved" |
| 6 | Phase 5 | Validation complete | Validation report | "fix" / "proceed" |
| 7 | Phase 6 | All changes written | Activation summary | Acknowledgment |

