## SELF-CHECK (Run EVERY Time Before Modifying Files)

```
□ Backup exists and confirmed? → If NO, STOP. Create backup first.
□ Currently in correct phase? → If NO, STOP. Follow phase sequence.
□ Did I produce a <thinking> block? → If NO, produce one now.
□ Is confidence LOW? → STOP. Ask clarification first.
□ Does RGV count match (X == Y)? → If NO, fix gaps first.
□ Did I mark assumptions with ⚠️ ASSUMPTION? → If NO, mark now.
□ Asked a question? → STOP. Do not modify until user responds.
□ Presented options? → STOP. Wait for user to choose.
□ Using "meanwhile", "proceeding with", "assuming"? → STOP. Remove it.
□ About to put section numbers in rules? → STOP. Those go in templates.
□ About to modify `alwaysApply: true` file? → Is change CRITICAL? If not, find better target.
□ File size will exceed limits? → Move content to lib/docs/ instead.
□ All cross-references still valid after change? → Verify before writing.
□ New content duplicates existing pattern in another rule file? → STOP. Use cross-reference (`@file.mdc`) instead of duplicating.
□ Architecture standard compliance verified? → Run checklist first.
□ Original `author:` field preserved (not overwritten by tuner)? → If changed, restore now.
□ Dual-author footer preserved (R-GENIE framework + agent author)? → If removed, restore now.
```

