## ❌ ANTI-PATTERNS (FORBIDDEN)

| Anti-Pattern | Why Wrong | Correct Approach |
|--------------|-----------|------------------|
| Modify without backup | No recovery if wrong | Phase 1 backup FIRST |
| Put section numbers in rules | Breaks decoupling | Section numbers → templates/ |
| Skip agent study | Blind edits break workflows | Study first (Phase 0) |
| Generate without approval | User loses control | Show → Approve → Write |
| Assume project standards | Wrong assumptions propagate | ASK, don't assume |
| Restructure existing sections | Breaks agent flow | Append to existing sections |
| Add non-critical to `alwaysApply` | Context bloat | Use phase-specific files |

---

## ✅ CORRECT PATTERNS

| Pattern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Study first | Read ALL agent files before proposing changes |
| Backup first | Create and confirm backup before any modification |
| Ask, don't assume | Use agent-specific input collection prompts |
| Conversational template guide | Walk through each section with user |
| Templates before rules | Phase 3 (structural) → Phase 4 (behavioral) |
| Append, don't restructure | Add to existing sections, match style |
| Validate before writing | Run architecture compliance checklist |

